  1370   * Whether the image is translucent or not is determined by the bottom layer's
  1371   * alpha channel. However, even if the bottom layer lacks an alpha channel,
  1372   * it can still have an opacity < 1. In this case, the QImage is promoted
  1373   * to 32-bit. (Note this is different from the output from the GIMP image
  1374   * exporter, which seems to ignore this attribute.)
  1375   *
  1376   * Independently, higher layers can be translucent, but the background of
  1377   * the image will not show through if the bottom layer is opaque.
  1378   *
  1379   * For indexed images, translucency is an all or nothing effect.
  1380   * \param xcf_image contains image info and bottom-most layer.
  1381   */
  1382  bool XCFImageFormat::initializeImage(XCFImage &xcf_image)
